## Explanation of the logic

The comment above the helper explains its purpose: pnpm 11 writes a two-document lockfile when `managePackageManagerVersions` is enabled — the first document holds package-manager metadata and the second holds the workspace lockfile. The code notes it will "always read the workspace document."

The selection logic works positionally:
- If the content does not begin with the document-start marker, it is treated as a single-document file and returned unchanged.
- Otherwise, it searches for the document separator (starting after the initial start marker) and returns the slice following that separator — i.e., the second (workspace) document.
- If no separator is found after the start marker, it returns an empty string.

